From: bherbruck <brennen.herbruck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:25:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: align a work offset 3-2-1 from a face, an edge and
 a vertex or bore

pick::align_321 reads the open operation's picks as datums: a flat face
sets Z (its outward normal), a straight edge sets X (projected into the
face's plane), a vertex or a bore's centre sets the origin (projected
onto the face; else the edge's start). The frame goes to the WCS pane's
slot through the existing undoable SetWcs command. The Geometry page
offers "Align WCS (3-2-1)" under the picks, dark with the refusal as
its tooltip until the picks qualify. Shell snapshots move by that
button only.

Fixes #187

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
